{
  "version": 1,
  "about": [
    "The golden fixture for the carried commit (mls/core/src/carried_commit.rs, docs/delivery.md §The carried commit).",
    "A leave is the one proposal a commit names by reference, and a member that never received a proposal cannot apply a commit that names it (RFC 9420 §12.4). So the committer sends the proposal messages it commits in the same entry as the commit, and a reader takes them first.",
    "carried = ff 4c 43 01 || n (1..=64) || n x (BE32(len) || proposal) || commit. A raw MLS message starts with its version, 00 01, so the two never collide.",
    "Every commit of a leave carries its proposals, and every build reads both forms.",
    "Written by an independent implementation (Python's struct), so the Rust replay is a second opinion. Replayed through the fixture door (kind \"carried_commit\") in Rust, JavaScript and Swift (and, in Peachy's Android client, Kotlin)."
  ],
